<div id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We already know from Remark <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem13" title="Remark 3.13. ‣ 3 Hubs-biased Laplacians and their spectra ‣ Hubs-biased resistance distances on graphs and networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.13</span></a> that <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\alpha=1,n}\leq\varDelta^{2}/\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\alpha=1,n}\leq\varDelta^{2}/\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha=1}(v)=k_{v}\sum_{j\in\eta_{v}}k_{j}^{-1}\leq\varDelta^{2}/\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha=1}(v)=k_{v}\sum_{j\in\eta_{v}}k_{j}^{-1}\leq\varDelta^{2}/\delta</annotation></semantics></math>
and using the Corollary <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Corollary 4.7. ‣ 4.1 Hubs-biased Kirchhoff index ‣ 4 Hubs-biased Resistance Distance ‣ Hubs-biased resistance distances on graphs and networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a> we obtain the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 4.10</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
